title The first free family, and a guard that had been reading nothing at all
prompt Autonomous loop -- Standfast on reds, then the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first on the Caravan lift arc
think Standfast pass first, run rather than recited: crux/REDS.md reads %140, %141, %142 each with a CLOSED row beneath it, so the line was clear before any constructive work opened.
think Council rota lap index: git log holds 3282 commits, 3282 mod 5 = 2, so row 2 -- Fire/Mars, cut and stop: Standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal.
think Priced lost_note off disk before touching it: forty rungs declare it, all forty wrote the same twelve-line body, and the harness imports none of the forty, so below_the_line=0 and every rung folds.
think Read the body's reaches by hand before lifting. Five names -- max_queue_len, phase_bit, seat_note, plan_name, NoteError -- and every one is declared in the rung itself and already pub, so the lift takes the rung as a comptime type parameter for all five and opens nothing.
think Wrote the lifted body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye, then replaced the identical twenty-three-line doc-and-body block in each of the forty rungs with a one-line doc and a three-line stub returning ladder_checks.lost_note(@This(), io, held, lost_mask).
think The sweep list was built by grepping for the signature AFTER appending the lifted body, so the harness matched its own new function and stubbed itself into infinite recursion. A count caught it -- forty-one files where forty were expected -- and the harness body was rewritten whole before any witness ran.
think Declined to book that near-miss. Nothing escaped, nothing was claimed, nothing was believed; it is REDS %111's lesson arriving in a new costume, and the ledger is for what got past a guard.
think Carry fell 65,180 to 64,829 -- exactly the predicted 351, the ninth exact hit in a row.
think Then read the carry witness's own GREEN line before rewriting it, and found it saying each of the twenty-two folding rungs for a lap that folded forty-four -- a sentence carried forward from the case_path lap and shipped in a signed send.
think Ran caravan_ladder_prose_count_scan.sh against that elder file from git show, in a temp directory: printed=0 verdict=ok. The guard that exists to hold exactly this property was reading nothing at all, because it extracts [0-9]+ runs and this arc spells its meter prose in words.
think REDS %142 wrote that lesson down one lap earlier in plain words -- a meter that reads digits sees half of what it is looking for -- and closed without building it. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom, so the loom is the closing.
think Measured before choosing the bound rather than guessing it: extracted spelled numbers across all five ladder meters and read the distribution. Ten and above gave five real hits; below ten gave twenty-five determiners like one body, two lines, five names.
think Set the bound at ten and reported the words below it as spelled_small rather than dropping them, since a scan that narrows its own subject must say so (REDS %102).
obs The honest reason a spelled-number rule can exist at all is that the numbers above ten in this prose are always measurements and the ones below are almost always determiners. That is a property of English rather than of this tree, and naming it in the scan header is what keeps the bound from reading as arbitrary.
obs Five living sites answered the loom on the lap it opened -- an eleven, two thirteens, a fifty, and a twelve. Four of them left their sentences and one earned nothing, because the fix is not a better number, it is no number, which is the scan's own oldest principle applied to its newest rule.
obs lost_note is the first family of this arc to lead the queue owing nothing to the harness import list. Every prior free fold was free because the harness happened to already import what the body reached; this one is free because the body reaches only what the folding rung itself publishes.
loom witness=caravan_ladder_carry_scan carry_before=65180 carry_after=64829 predicted=351 realized=351 families=703 modules=110
loom witness=ladder_reach_visibility_scan family=lost_note folding=40 widens=0 stub=3 fall=351
loom witness=caravan_ladder_prose_count_scan printed=23 spelled=5 spelled_small=24 verdict=ok
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the lifted lost_note body, one published function over a comptime rung parameter
file caravan/amend.rye one of forty rungs whose twelve-line body became a three-line stub
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_prose_count_scan.sh the spelled-number reader, bounded at ten, with the words below it reported
file tools/caravan_ladder_copy_witness.rish three legs proving the spelled bound on generated controls
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish ceiling down to 64,829 and both narrative lines rewritten to this lap's truth
file tools/caravan_ladder_reach_visibility_witness.rish window slid forward one family, sink corpus and farewell holding moved with the fold
file crux/REDS.md %143 booked and closed, headline moved in the same edit
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refilled with the live work, prior edge folded down to one line
recommend keep-going judge_outcome is the next honest head -- thirty-seven rungs of sixteen lines returning 468, half its seventy-four widenings free import bindings of carry and half of them struct openings the meter learned to see this week
